[statement]
A name narrows another only where every candidate of it holds the other:
`z`, a candidate for `w` with a priority, does not hold `d`, and `d`
takes its best candidate, `d` 3; `w` then takes `z`. Contrast
`a-name-every-candidate-of-which-holds-another-narrows-its-choice`.

[repository]
P:d
V:1
p:w

P:d
V:2
p:w

P:z
V:1
k:1
p:w

P:d
V:3

[request]
w
d

[answer apk-tools 3.0.9-r0]
install d 3
install z 1
